1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:02,230
[Characters, behaviors, places, organizations,
professions, or events shown in the series

2
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:03,500
are entirely fictional,
solely for the purpose of entertainment,

3
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:04,770
with no intention to instruct
or promote any kind of behavior;

4
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:06,040
viewer discretion is advised]

5
00:00:06,130 --> 00:00:08,520
I made you breakfast.

6
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:14,400
When afflictions come your way,

7
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:16,640
even I cannot come to your rescue.

8
00:00:20,070 --> 00:00:22,000
Never.

9
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,390
Dear vital spirits.

10
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:31,040
My dearest,

11
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:34,320
stay here with me.

12
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:48,640
Cursed with black magic...
[Been put under a love spell]

13
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:50,030
[The signs of being under a love spell,
or Ya Faed charm,

14
00:01:50,050 --> 00:01:51,060
can be seen through
significant changes

15
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:51,880
in behavior and emotion]

16
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:54,430
[For Saneh Ya Faed, beware of food]

17
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:00,120
At the station...

18
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:28,880
I was just going to wake you up.

19
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:32,550
Where are you rushing off to?

20
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,320
Come here.

21
00:02:48,830 --> 00:02:51,600
I woke up before daybreak to cook.

22
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:56,390
No, I'm fine, thanks.

23
00:02:56,790 --> 00:02:58,600
I already told you

24
00:02:58,860 --> 00:03:01,120
I don't eat breakfast.

25
00:03:12,090 --> 00:03:13,510
Just have a taste.

26
00:03:27,090 --> 00:03:28,410
I'm good.

27
00:03:28,650 --> 00:03:29,680
It'll be such a waste.

28
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:32,070
What you yourself cook

29
00:03:32,090 --> 00:03:34,600
is never as delightful
as when someone cooks with you in mind.

30
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:36,960
Very well, then.

31
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,920
I will make you coffee.

32
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:41,520
I'd rather not.

33
00:03:41,910 --> 00:03:45,000
I'll find something
to drink near the station.

34
00:03:45,670 --> 00:03:46,840
I don't wanna bother you.

35
00:03:52,610 --> 00:03:55,690
Had those words not come from
someone with whom I shared a bed,

36
00:03:56,510 --> 00:03:58,640
I would have thought
you found me abhorrent.

37
00:03:59,610 --> 00:04:00,500
It's...

38
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:04,500
It's not like that.

39
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,870
I just...

40
00:04:05,890 --> 00:04:07,910
don't usually eat...

41
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:34,470
Be it lunch or an afternoon meal,

42
00:04:35,130 --> 00:04:36,960
as you wish, Officer.

43
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:51,600
I do not usually dine at supper,

44
00:04:52,830 --> 00:04:54,700
but I shall prepare a meal set for you.

45
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:35,990
♫Along with ghostly spirits
hounding relentlessly,♫

46
00:05:36,010 --> 00:05:40,730
♫May the maras be ravaged
and perish completely♫

47
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:44,910
♫Vindictive spirits, tyrannical psyches,♫

48
00:05:44,950 --> 00:05:49,250
♫Meant to betray, slaughter, and invade,♫

49
00:05:49,270 --> 00:05:53,650
♫Were any souls to brush
against my karmic soulmate,♫

50
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:58,360
♫They shall bury the thought
of returning to their realm♫

51
00:05:58,390 --> 00:06:02,410
♫With incantation and virtue as shield,♫

52
00:06:02,430 --> 00:06:06,880
♫At my feet,
they shall surrender and kneel,♫

53
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:12,000
♫Chanting, "Sadhu," of their own will♫

54
00:06:36,210 --> 00:06:37,010
The suspects?

55
00:06:37,030 --> 00:06:37,830
Exactly.

56
00:06:38,810 --> 00:06:39,810
Tons.

57
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:42,310
"Be it lunch or an afternoon meal,"

58
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:44,620
"as you wish, Officer."

59
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:46,720
Oh,

60
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:49,800
the premium tiffin is back.

61
00:06:52,810 --> 00:06:54,800
If you wanna eat it, feel free to take it.

62
00:06:55,510 --> 00:06:56,670
It's all yours.

63
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,010
Won't your partner get mad?

64
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:04,660
You should really use these bait questions

65
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:06,300
during investigations.

66
00:07:06,610 --> 00:07:07,780
I think...

67
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:09,780
you'll get a promotion in no time.

68
00:07:09,810 --> 00:07:11,100
Oh, that mouth.

69
00:07:11,790 --> 00:07:12,520
I'll take it, ma'am.

70
00:07:13,010 --> 00:07:13,820
Alright.

71
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:17,360
Feel free to eat it if you're hungry.

72
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:22,990
What's on the menu today?

73
00:07:23,310 --> 00:07:24,610
Oh...

74
00:07:26,010 --> 00:07:27,170
Oh!

75
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:31,090
There are grapes, too.

76
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:33,220
Wow...

77
00:07:39,810 --> 00:07:41,190
These are hard to come by.

78
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:45,710
Mm!

79
00:07:46,410 --> 00:07:47,410
Scrumptious, Lieutenant.

80
00:07:51,550 --> 00:07:52,550
Sarge,

81
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:55,310
can I ask you something?

82
00:07:55,390 --> 00:07:56,390
Yes, ma'am.

83
00:07:56,810 --> 00:07:59,830
Being cursed with black magic...

84
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:01,820
or the dark arts,

85
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,400
that...is real, right?

86
00:08:04,610 --> 00:08:05,610
It exists.

87
00:08:06,070 --> 00:08:08,080
There was a man from the Northeast

88
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:09,840
who got so hung up on a woman here

89
00:08:09,910 --> 00:08:11,290
that he transferred here for work

90
00:08:11,310 --> 00:08:12,360
and never left.

91
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Really, Sarge?

92
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:15,010
Really.

93
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:16,410
Who is he?

94
00:08:16,430 --> 00:08:17,320
That's me.

95
00:08:17,810 --> 00:08:20,420
Take it from my wife,
who got the great charm of metta and favor

96
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:21,810
tattooed by the Master.

97
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:24,840
Nowadays, we still
go at it hard after work.

98
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:26,010
Be serious.

99
00:08:26,630 --> 00:08:28,120
I'm not freaking kidding, Sarge.

100
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:29,660
I mean,

101
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:31,420
superstars get tattoos from her, too.

102
00:08:31,450 --> 00:08:32,910
She has tons of disciples.

103
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:34,950
If you're interested,

104
00:08:34,970 --> 00:08:36,760
I can ask my wife to pull some strings.

105
00:08:38,700 --> 00:08:39,990
I'd rather not, Sarge.

106
00:08:40,010 --> 00:08:41,080
I think...

107
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:42,610
I'm good with what I have.

108
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,360
Though...

109
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:47,800
what I'm curious about is...

110
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:51,690
she has that many disciples,

111
00:08:51,710 --> 00:08:53,520
and each of them

112
00:08:53,890 --> 00:08:56,140
is a famous superstar or actress.

113
00:08:56,300 --> 00:08:57,080
That means

114
00:08:57,100 --> 00:09:00,000
she must have made a lot from ritual fees.

115
00:09:00,030 --> 00:09:02,360
That's why she could build
such a ginormous house, right?

116
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:04,120
Don't say things like that, Lieutenant.

117
00:09:04,470 --> 00:09:05,400
With her,

118
00:09:05,610 --> 00:09:08,040
if you ask about a ritual fee

119
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:09,700
or her pay,

120
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,040
she gets real angry.

121
00:09:11,430 --> 00:09:13,270
She's been doing it
since her father's time.

122
00:09:13,290 --> 00:09:15,200
She's helped both the rich and the poor.

123
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:17,640
Otherwise, she'd be a billionaire.

124
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:18,310
Mm.

125
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:20,290
My wife asked

126
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:22,660
if you didn't spend
the night at the residence.

127
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:24,400
She knocked for a long time.

128
00:09:28,510 --> 00:09:29,720
Ah, it's okay.

129
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:30,720
I get it.

130
00:09:30,940 --> 00:09:32,290
Everyone who comes to

131
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,520
the police quarters sees it.

132
00:09:38,050 --> 00:09:41,820
Do you have any accommodations
you can recommend?

133
00:09:41,850 --> 00:09:46,080
I want the one with
a three- or six-month lease.

134
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:48,200
I have some.

135
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:49,940
Let me finish this first.

136
00:09:50,870 --> 00:09:52,400
Your partner did a great job.

137
00:09:53,010 --> 00:09:54,290
Not my partner.

138
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,280
I don't have a partner.

139
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:56,300
You don't?

140
00:09:56,730 --> 00:09:57,720
Serves you right.

141
00:09:58,480 --> 00:09:59,680
Just stay single.

142
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:01,420
Sorry, ma'am.

143
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:19,390
Thank you so much, Master.

144
00:10:20,190 --> 00:10:21,480
How is the child?

145
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:24,460
She's doing better,

146
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:27,790
but we're letting her stay on leave

147
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:30,400
until she's mentally ready to come back.

148
00:10:31,210 --> 00:10:34,000
She may have a fever or body aches.

149
00:10:34,020 --> 00:10:36,200
Give her some medicine
and tell her to rest.

150
00:10:36,220 --> 00:10:38,040
She will return to
her normal self within three days.

151
00:10:38,710 --> 00:10:39,990
Yes, Master.

152
00:10:40,230 --> 00:10:42,320
Thank you very much again, Master.

153
00:10:43,610 --> 00:10:46,150
I'll go tell her guardians right away

154
00:10:46,170 --> 00:10:47,720
to put their minds at ease.

155
00:10:51,370 --> 00:10:52,910
On the day of the incident,

156
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:56,480
the lieutenant merely did
what a good officer ought to.

157
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:58,580
Do not hold it against her.

158
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:02,000
Yes, Master.

159
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:04,310
People have been talking on and on

160
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:06,090
about this new policewoman.

161
00:11:06,590 --> 00:11:08,680
But if you, Master, insist,

162
00:11:08,730 --> 00:11:10,490
I'm relieved.

163
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:13,600
I myself do not hold it against her.

164
00:11:13,630 --> 00:11:15,080
Hence, others should not.

165
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:18,480
We must also thank her for her courage.

166
00:11:20,310 --> 00:11:22,320
Do you understand
what I am saying, Miss?

167
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,580
I do.

168
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,960
In fact...

169
00:11:27,430 --> 00:11:30,200
the child's mother asked me
to thank the officer on her behalf.

170
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:31,720
Though I

171
00:11:31,740 --> 00:11:34,200
haven't had time to stop by the station.

172
00:11:34,810 --> 00:11:38,190
I was going to give her stuff back.

173
00:11:39,060 --> 00:11:42,300
Whatever of hers is dropped here

174
00:11:42,330 --> 00:11:44,320
or anywhere hereafter,

175
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:47,120
leave it only in my care.

176
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:49,480
Oh, yes.

177
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:24,720
Hello.

178
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:28,270
Do you have a room for monthly rent?

179
00:12:28,290 --> 00:12:30,000
Let me check for you, ma'am.

180
00:12:38,350 --> 00:12:39,350
Hello, Sarge.

181
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:40,520
How's it going, Lieutenant?

182
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:41,780
Did you get a room?

183
00:12:42,610 --> 00:12:44,390
That place is the best in the district.

184
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:47,000
I'm waiting for the staff
to take a look, Sarge.

185
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:49,620
I'm sorry, but we have no vacancies.

186
00:12:50,950 --> 00:12:52,200
- It's okay. Thank you.
- You're welcome.

187
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:53,000
Thank you.

188
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:54,680
There goes the first one, Sarge.

189
00:12:58,780 --> 00:13:00,040
There's a dog here?

190
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:01,880
Hello.

191
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:02,850
Hello, beautiful.

192
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:04,960
I'm looking for a monthly rental.

193
00:13:05,710 --> 00:13:06,710
Give me a sec.

194
00:13:07,610 --> 00:13:08,400
Hello?

195
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:09,600
Huh!

196
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:12,080
The water isn't running, the power is out,
and the A/C's not cooling?

197
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,030
I'll send our guy to take care of it.

198
00:13:14,050 --> 00:13:15,180
It'll take just a sec.

199
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:15,740
Alright.

200
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:16,450
Alright, alright.

201
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,240
You were saying?

202
00:13:18,350 --> 00:13:20,350
The water isn't running well?

203
00:13:20,370 --> 00:13:22,300
It's crystal clear. No worries.

204
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,320
It runs every day.

205
00:13:24,620 --> 00:13:26,480
And the A/C isn't cooling well?

206
00:13:27,330 --> 00:13:29,840
Again, no worries. Every room
is nice and cold. Down to 18 degrees.

207
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:33,040
You seem to be
breaking out in a sweat there.

208
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:34,620
This is normal.

209
00:13:38,510 --> 00:13:39,640
Hello, Sarge.

210
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:42,520
This place...

211
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:44,410
doesn't really work.

212
00:13:44,830 --> 00:13:46,670
The staff seems weirdly confused.

213
00:13:46,690 --> 00:13:47,400
The A/Cs aren't even doing anything.

214
00:13:47,440 --> 00:13:49,380
He's real confused, the staff here.

215
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:50,880
He's eating rice with limes!

216
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:52,400
Feel free to take a look.

217
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,840
- So if I want to sign a lease...
- Hold on, hold on a sec.

218
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:58,010
Hi there.

219
00:13:58,030 --> 00:14:00,020
Who is this?

220
00:14:00,630 --> 00:14:02,080
Oh... Ooh!

221
00:14:02,510 --> 00:14:04,690
You're confirming and paying the deposit?

222
00:14:06,830 --> 00:14:09,860
Sure thing. Okay.

223
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:11,790
Sure thing. See you.

224
00:14:11,810 --> 00:14:12,440
Alrighty.

225
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:14,600
If I'm ready to sign a lease here...

226
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:15,760
We're fully booked!

227
00:14:17,830 --> 00:14:19,860
But if you're interested
in reserving a room,

228
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:22,160
you can wire me the deposit in advance.

229
00:14:22,250 --> 00:14:24,320
Where's your ID card?

230
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:26,920
If you wire the money to my account,

231
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:28,680
I'll lower the rent to 500 baht.

232
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:30,900
From 10,000, so think carefully.

233
00:14:30,920 --> 00:14:31,760
Think!

234
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:34,280
Just think. Wire it to my account. It's...

235
00:14:35,110 --> 00:14:36,920
Though...what do you do for a living?

236
00:14:37,540 --> 00:14:38,600
I'm a cop.

237
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,040
A what now?

238
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:41,360
A cop.

239
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:43,910
Just wire it to
this place's account, then, sweetie.

240
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:45,350
You seem friendly, Auntie.

241
00:14:45,370 --> 00:14:46,290
I am friendly, sweetie.

242
00:14:46,310 --> 00:14:47,310
Friendly for a swindle, that is.

243
00:14:47,330 --> 00:14:48,990
Huh? A swind-what?

244
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:53,090
Hello, it's Plaifah again today,

245
00:14:53,110 --> 00:14:54,460
along with my friend.

246
00:14:54,490 --> 00:14:55,030
What's your name again?

247
00:14:55,050 --> 00:14:56,790
My name is Book.

248
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:01,620
Let's read your comments.

249
00:15:01,790 --> 00:15:03,390
They're saying I'm prettier
than you, that's it.

250
00:15:03,410 --> 00:15:04,480
Not true.
[Grilled Pork Station]

251
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:05,750
- Guys, let's not lie to her.
- Uh...

252
00:15:05,770 --> 00:15:07,770
Don't get her hopes up.

253
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:10,320
Auntie, I'd like three chicken skewers.

254
00:15:12,190 --> 00:15:12,960
Girl, look.

255
00:15:17,410 --> 00:15:19,200
What is this one, Auntie?

256
00:15:19,230 --> 00:15:21,510
- Grilled marinated pork.
- Oh, pork.

257
00:15:25,490 --> 00:15:26,980
What's your name?

258
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,220
Can I have your Insta?

259
00:15:30,110 --> 00:15:31,760
I'm not on social media.

260
00:15:32,090 --> 00:15:34,840
Then, your number, please!

261
00:15:34,860 --> 00:15:36,190
Pwease, pwease, pwease.

262
00:15:37,100 --> 00:15:39,200
I don't just give my number out to anyone.

263
00:15:40,970 --> 00:15:43,430
You're playing hard to get.

264
00:15:45,190 --> 00:15:46,190
Good!

265
00:15:46,210 --> 00:15:47,480
Someone who's hard to win over

266
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:49,180
is just my type!

267
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:51,820
- Let go.
- No, I won't.

268
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:54,510
- Kid, let go.
- As if I'd let go of someone so slick.

269
00:15:58,090 --> 00:16:00,110
Hey...what are you girls doing?

270
00:16:00,130 --> 00:16:00,880
Oh,

271
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:03,370
we're going live, creating some content.

272
00:16:03,390 --> 00:16:04,900
I'm Plaifah.

273
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:06,290
What's your name?

274
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:07,950
Priew!

275
00:16:07,970 --> 00:16:09,510
Your darling commented that

276
00:16:09,530 --> 00:16:11,290
you're making
a fool out of her by cheating.

277
00:16:11,550 --> 00:16:13,120
Since when did I do that?

278
00:16:13,150 --> 00:16:15,210
She was born a fool.

279
00:16:15,230 --> 00:16:16,330
Stephan,

280
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:17,260
you dumbass!

281
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:19,170
I've never made a fool out of you

282
00:16:19,190 --> 00:16:19,670
because you

283
00:16:19,690 --> 00:16:21,520
have always been one!

284
00:16:21,810 --> 00:16:22,630
And this...

285
00:16:22,650 --> 00:16:23,880
is my new girl!

286
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:25,170
She's...

287
00:16:25,190 --> 00:16:26,490
What is your name?

288
00:16:28,090 --> 00:16:28,560
Peem.

289
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:30,690
She's Peem!

290
00:16:30,710 --> 00:16:32,340
She looks good,

291
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:33,690
has a nice body,

292
00:16:33,710 --> 00:16:35,770
and her skin is so fair!

293
00:16:35,790 --> 00:16:38,000
She looks like she takes 10 showers a day.

294
00:16:38,430 --> 00:16:39,430
Someone like you

295
00:16:39,450 --> 00:16:41,070
could never compare.

296
00:16:41,090 --> 00:16:42,630
All you do is ride a motorcycle all day,

297
00:16:42,650 --> 00:16:44,490
revving and revving.

298
00:16:44,510 --> 00:16:46,610
Not fabulous!

299
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:49,420
Are you done now?

300
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:52,380
- If you are, please let go.
- No, I'm not letting go!

301
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:54,200
I still want to talk to you, Peem.

302
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:01,800
Hey, Miss!

303
00:17:01,820 --> 00:17:04,400
Let go of my girl right now.

304
00:17:04,710 --> 00:17:07,910
Don't say I didn't warn ya!

305
00:17:08,140 --> 00:17:09,000
Who's your girl?!

306
00:17:09,020 --> 00:17:10,410
I already broke up with you this morning.

307
00:17:10,430 --> 00:17:12,120
And this is my new girl!

308
00:17:25,950 --> 00:17:27,400
That doesn't freaking count!

309
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:28,850
I freaking warned ya!

310
00:17:28,870 --> 00:17:29,910
Let go of her.

311
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:31,680
I'm not holding her.

312
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:33,920
There, you're doing it.

313
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:36,890
Pointing fingers, huh?

314
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:39,840
If you're just bickering, be my guest.

315
00:17:40,620 --> 00:17:42,570
But if you're gonna fight,

316
00:17:42,590 --> 00:17:43,260
good!

317
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,950
I'm taking you all in
for an attitude adjustment.

318
00:17:46,150 --> 00:17:47,030
Are you a teacher?

319
00:17:47,140 --> 00:17:47,880
I'm not a teacher.

320
00:17:47,950 --> 00:17:48,760
Oh, what are you?

321
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:50,000
A "cop."

322
00:17:51,230 --> 00:17:51,830
Whoa!

323
00:17:51,850 --> 00:17:53,880
My dad's a cop too, just so you know.

324
00:17:54,060 --> 00:17:54,830
There's no way

325
00:17:54,850 --> 00:17:56,570
I'm letting you slip through
my fingers that easily.

326
00:17:56,590 --> 00:17:57,910
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

327
00:17:57,930 --> 00:17:59,910
Ugh, Stephan, let go! Let go!

328
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:01,920
So you're not listening
to a word I'm saying?

329
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:03,290
Why is an outsider

330
00:18:04,150 --> 00:18:05,150
sticking her nose in?!

331
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:06,090
This is between...

332
00:18:06,110 --> 00:18:06,990
Ow, ow!

333
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:08,200
Ow!

334
00:18:16,110 --> 00:18:17,720
That was crisp.

335
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:18,920
Totally my type.

336
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:23,290
My first time feeling like a bottom.

337
00:18:25,130 --> 00:18:25,760
What's the matter?

338
00:18:26,010 --> 00:18:27,700
I'm a bottom, that's what.

339
00:18:29,316 --> 00:18:30,046
So cute!

340
00:18:30,070 --> 00:18:31,190
What a boss!

341
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:36,170
And you modded your motorcycle.

342
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:39,410
Do you know it's against the law
to modify a vehicle?

343
00:18:39,900 --> 00:18:40,690
Good.

344
00:18:40,910 --> 00:18:42,900
You'll get fined at the station.

345
00:18:43,610 --> 00:18:44,310
Miss...

346
00:18:44,330 --> 00:18:45,430
Don't fine me.

347
00:18:45,450 --> 00:18:47,120
Please don't fine me.

348
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:49,520
I'm so sorry, Miss.

349
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:51,000
Please don't do anything to me.

350
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:52,530
I'm just a cute, wittle baby.

351
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:53,370
Please don't.

352
00:18:53,390 --> 00:18:54,670
Please give her some grace.

353
00:18:54,690 --> 00:18:55,840
- She doesn't have a dime.
- Mm.

354
00:18:56,090 --> 00:18:58,220
She's spent all the money
modding the motorcycle.

355
00:18:58,240 --> 00:18:59,590
Just help her.

356
00:18:59,610 --> 00:19:00,480
Please?

357
00:19:00,890 --> 00:19:02,760
For her red hair's sake.

358
00:19:03,410 --> 00:19:04,690
Please, Peem?

359
00:19:04,710 --> 00:19:05,380
Sure.

360
00:19:08,540 --> 00:19:09,600
Sergeant, go.

361
00:19:09,620 --> 00:19:12,090
- You said you weren't gonna arrest me!
- Stephan!

362
00:19:12,220 --> 00:19:13,350
Stephan!

363
00:19:13,370 --> 00:19:15,100
Stephan!

364
00:19:15,120 --> 00:19:15,840
Stephan!

365
00:19:19,930 --> 00:19:20,600
Miss!

366
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:22,510
How am I gonna go home?

367
00:19:22,530 --> 00:19:24,450
Could you give me a ride home?

368
00:19:24,460 --> 00:19:25,460
Please?

369
00:19:26,190 --> 00:19:27,710
Why didn't you call
your guardians to do that?

370
00:19:27,980 --> 00:19:29,060
Whoa...

371
00:19:29,350 --> 00:19:30,960
If I call them,

372
00:19:30,990 --> 00:19:33,090
I'll never hear the end of it.

373
00:19:33,110 --> 00:19:34,370
I'm not doing that.

374
00:19:34,390 --> 00:19:37,110
Give me a ride home, please.

375
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:40,320
Give me directions. I'll give you a ride.

376
00:19:40,690 --> 00:19:42,130
How cute!

377
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:42,980
Oh, whoa... Damn it.

378
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,110
- Priew!
- Priew!

379
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:45,800
- We can give you a ride!
- We can give you a ride!

380
00:19:46,300 --> 00:19:47,510
What? I'm going with Peem!

381
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:50,550
- What? How could you just dump us?!
- I'm going with Peem!

382
00:19:50,570 --> 00:19:51,240
Get lost!

383
00:19:53,580 --> 00:19:55,130
Thank you so much, Peem,

384
00:19:55,150 --> 00:19:57,690
for giving me a ride.

385
00:19:58,810 --> 00:19:59,940
And...

386
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:01,270
someone's home, right?

387
00:20:02,490 --> 00:20:04,890
My parents are probably inside.

388
00:20:04,910 --> 00:20:06,880
I'm not so sure.

389
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:08,790
Can I go home with you?

390
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:11,390
I'd rather not, Priew.

391
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:12,590
By the way...

392
00:20:12,710 --> 00:20:14,310
speaking of the motorcycle,

393
00:20:14,810 --> 00:20:16,870
can you pass the message along
to your girlfriend

394
00:20:17,090 --> 00:20:18,640
that if she behaves herself

395
00:20:18,650 --> 00:20:19,230
and...

396
00:20:19,370 --> 00:20:21,080
promises me

397
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:24,200
she'll reverse the modifications,

398
00:20:24,610 --> 00:20:25,900
I'll return the motorcycle to her.

399
00:20:26,170 --> 00:20:28,590
As for the fine,

400
00:20:28,890 --> 00:20:29,890
I'll...

401
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:33,190
have a word with your guardians later.

402
00:20:33,210 --> 00:20:35,280
If you behave yourself,

403
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:36,580
I won't fine you.

404
00:20:37,190 --> 00:20:38,120
Understood?

405
00:20:38,140 --> 00:20:39,900
Okay, okay!

406
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:41,500
Then...wait here for a bit.

407
00:20:41,520 --> 00:20:42,490
I'll call my dad for you.

408
00:20:42,510 --> 00:20:44,110
Just a second!

409
00:20:46,410 --> 00:20:47,160
Dad!

410
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:49,500
Dad, open the door for me!

411
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,100
Are you home?!

412
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:52,070
Dad!

413
00:20:52,090 --> 00:20:53,320
- I'm here!
- Ooh...

414
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:55,030
Whoa, Sarge!

415
00:20:56,010 --> 00:20:57,010
Oh?

416
00:20:57,690 --> 00:20:58,620
What are you doing here, Lieutenant?

417
00:20:59,790 --> 00:21:01,200
Is she...your daughter?

418
00:21:01,310 --> 00:21:02,230
She is.

419
00:21:02,250 --> 00:21:02,860
My daughter.

420
00:21:02,880 --> 00:21:04,690
And why are you out here?

421
00:21:05,790 --> 00:21:07,070
- I can't get inside, sweetie.
- What?

422
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:08,830
Why can't you?!

423
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:10,490
I'm busted, sweetie.

424
00:21:12,190 --> 00:21:13,490
- Ugh, just stop...
- Sarge, do you know

425
00:21:13,510 --> 00:21:15,680
what a troublemaker she's been?

426
00:21:18,140 --> 00:21:19,140
Tell me about it later.

427
00:21:20,790 --> 00:21:21,830
Lieutenant...

428
00:21:21,850 --> 00:21:22,980
please call my wife over to help.

429
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,000
I wanna get inside.

430
00:21:24,390 --> 00:21:25,670
Why don't you call her yourself?

431
00:21:25,690 --> 00:21:26,780
She won't... She won't open the door.

432
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:28,890
Please help us. I wanna get inside.

433
00:21:31,910 --> 00:21:32,910
- Go all out, Lieutenant.
- Want some?

434
00:21:33,210 --> 00:21:34,280
- Consider it a welcome dinner.
- Want some?

435
00:21:35,180 --> 00:21:36,700
My hubby told me

436
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:38,810
you've been feeding him.

437
00:21:38,830 --> 00:21:41,800
- He's been well-fed for two days now
- You want anything?

438
00:21:41,820 --> 00:21:43,850
Thank you. Please eat a ton today.

439
00:21:43,870 --> 00:21:44,380
Come on.

440
00:21:44,410 --> 00:21:46,700
I'm the one who should be thanking him.

441
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:49,960
- Get this, I just transferred here.
- Eat some veggies...

442
00:21:49,980 --> 00:21:52,080
There are still so many things
I have to get used to.

443
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:53,790
I'm lucky to have him.

444
00:21:53,810 --> 00:21:55,440
Otherwise,
I'd be in a really tough spot.

445
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:58,080
When I first moved here,
I was just like you.

446
00:21:58,100 --> 00:22:00,590
But someone helped me adapt.

447
00:22:02,890 --> 00:22:04,670
- Wear some nice PJ tonight.
- Ugh!

448
00:22:04,700 --> 00:22:06,030
At this age,

449
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:07,870
you don't have to be so lovey-dovey.

450
00:22:07,890 --> 00:22:09,520
It's okay to take it down a notch.

451
00:22:09,540 --> 00:22:11,030
I'm so tired of raising this one.

452
00:22:11,790 --> 00:22:13,790
I'm the only one raising him.

453
00:22:13,810 --> 00:22:15,260
You're always out and about.

454
00:22:15,280 --> 00:22:16,800
Never once have you given me a hand.

455
00:22:16,830 --> 00:22:18,100
Damn you...Priew!

456
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:21,990
Priew...

457
00:22:22,300 --> 00:22:23,300
What?

458
00:22:23,390 --> 00:22:25,100
You told me your name was Plaifah.

459
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:26,130
Well, my name's Plaifah.

460
00:22:26,150 --> 00:22:27,270
Good grief!

461
00:22:27,290 --> 00:22:29,500
"Plaifah," my foot, Lieutenant.

462
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:31,030
This girl's damn name is Priew!

463
00:22:31,290 --> 00:22:32,800
When I was pregnant,

464
00:22:32,830 --> 00:22:35,330
I always craved limes,
mangoes, and all that sour stuff,

465
00:22:35,350 --> 00:22:37,100
so I named her "Priew," which means "sour."

466
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:38,670
That's not true, Lieutenant.
I'm still Plaifah.

467
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:39,620
Don't believe her.

468
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:41,150
Priew.

469
00:22:41,170 --> 00:22:41,740
Mom!

470
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:42,820
And you,

471
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:44,130
don't be so slutty.

472
00:22:44,150 --> 00:22:46,290
People are gonna say
your dad didn't discipline you!

473
00:22:46,310 --> 00:22:47,090
I am,

474
00:22:47,110 --> 00:22:47,940
but she wouldn't listen.

475
00:22:47,960 --> 00:22:48,960
Well, get it through her thick skull!

476
00:22:48,980 --> 00:22:50,020
- Discipline her until she listens!
- Ugh...

477
00:22:50,040 --> 00:22:51,400
Stop, stop, stop.

478
00:22:51,420 --> 00:22:53,630
It's genetic, you know?

479
00:22:53,870 --> 00:22:54,900
Like mother,

480
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:56,560
like daughter, Mommy.

481
00:22:56,710 --> 00:22:58,090
- Don't badmouth my wifey.
- This kid!

482
00:22:58,190 --> 00:22:59,480
Deal with her!

483
00:23:00,390 --> 00:23:01,390
Do it. Now!

484
00:23:01,410 --> 00:23:02,650
Oh, I'll do it to you tonight.

485
00:23:02,670 --> 00:23:03,130
Do what?

486
00:23:03,150 --> 00:23:03,900
- You'll definitely get some.
- Peem, want me to feed you?

487
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:04,530
Do what?

488
00:23:04,550 --> 00:23:05,730
- Our third kid is on the way.
- I'm good.

489
00:23:06,540 --> 00:23:07,780
Darling...

490
00:23:08,310 --> 00:23:09,580
Okay, I'll go shower while I wait.

491
00:23:09,600 --> 00:23:10,390
Props,

492
00:23:10,420 --> 00:23:12,190
get up, sweetie. Go on.

493
00:23:12,370 --> 00:23:14,680
- Yeah, I'll give it to you hard.
- Cover your ears, cover your ears.

494
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:17,230
I'll slam it like, "Bam, bam, bam, bam."

495
00:23:17,250 --> 00:23:18,790
Jeez, I'm not getting any sleep that way.

496
00:23:18,820 --> 00:23:19,940
I'll make sure you can't walk.

497
00:23:19,960 --> 00:23:21,380
- Kiddos,
- Go on. Let me put on my shoes first.

498
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:23,080
if you hear anything tonight,
don't get curious.

499
00:23:23,100 --> 00:23:24,180
Ugh!

500
00:23:25,090 --> 00:23:25,690
Hey,

501
00:23:26,460 --> 00:23:28,370
don't you feel
protective of your daughter?

502
00:23:28,390 --> 00:23:29,890
She's a young girl.

503
00:23:29,910 --> 00:23:32,200
Look how short her shorts were,

504
00:23:32,220 --> 00:23:34,030
not to mention how late she gets home.

505
00:23:34,380 --> 00:23:35,380
I'm...

506
00:23:35,700 --> 00:23:37,370
not protective, but I sure am worried.

507
00:23:38,700 --> 00:23:40,290
With that faux-hawk butch of hers,

508
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:41,710
they fight every day.

509
00:23:42,210 --> 00:23:43,210
Though...

510
00:23:43,370 --> 00:23:44,410
they always get back together.

511
00:23:44,900 --> 00:23:45,900
They...

512
00:23:46,180 --> 00:23:47,180
can never truly let each other go.

513
00:23:50,750 --> 00:23:51,750
The reason...

514
00:23:51,900 --> 00:23:53,630
they can't do that

515
00:23:53,650 --> 00:23:55,540
might be because...

516
00:23:55,740 --> 00:23:58,330
they're a safe space

517
00:23:58,340 --> 00:24:00,110
for each other.

518
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:01,810
Otherwise...

519
00:24:01,830 --> 00:24:04,080
they wouldn't keep
coming back to each other.

520
00:24:05,270 --> 00:24:06,880
Right, Sarge.

521
00:24:07,910 --> 00:24:11,120
Can I ask you a question?

522
00:24:14,770 --> 00:24:16,160
Why...

523
00:24:16,180 --> 00:24:18,560
did you decide to move to Phop Phra?

524
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:22,180
I've transferred to many locations.

525
00:24:23,190 --> 00:24:25,300
I...was a stray.

526
00:24:25,690 --> 00:24:27,030
I had nowhere to settle,

527
00:24:27,290 --> 00:24:28,790
so I built my own family here.

528
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:31,080
I think sometimes,

529
00:24:31,100 --> 00:24:33,710
it's about having a safe space,
like you said.

530
00:24:34,890 --> 00:24:36,240
A place called home.

531
00:24:37,980 --> 00:24:39,700
But a home isn't just a place.

532
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:41,480
It's where...

533
00:24:42,350 --> 00:24:43,300
the people who love you,

534
00:24:44,340 --> 00:24:45,480
and the people you love,

535
00:24:46,010 --> 00:24:47,010
are waiting.

536
00:24:49,800 --> 00:24:51,100
I suspect

537
00:24:51,120 --> 00:24:52,670
you're asking this because

538
00:24:53,990 --> 00:24:56,150
you've started
to take a liking to someone here?

539
00:24:58,770 --> 00:24:59,940
Aha!

540
00:25:03,010 --> 00:25:04,600
There's no one, Sarge.

541
00:25:06,070 --> 00:25:07,070
Eat your food.

542
00:25:07,090 --> 00:25:08,990
Is there no one,
or are you just not sure?

543
00:25:09,780 --> 00:25:10,880
Who are you into?

544
00:25:12,490 --> 00:25:13,380
Who?

545
00:25:13,400 --> 00:25:14,820
Who's the lucky one?

546
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:17,280
No one!

547
00:25:18,490 --> 00:25:20,880
Anyway, where are you
gonna spend the night?

548
00:25:30,010 --> 00:25:30,690
Sarge.

549
00:25:30,850 --> 00:25:31,370
Yes?

550
00:25:31,390 --> 00:25:32,380
Pass me the beer.

551
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:33,800
What?

552
00:25:33,980 --> 00:25:35,320
You said you didn't drink, though.

553
00:25:36,250 --> 00:25:36,980
Well...

554
00:25:37,600 --> 00:25:39,080
I changed my mind.

555
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:41,470
- Oh...
- Come on.

556
00:25:42,700 --> 00:25:44,010
Who are you seeing?

557
00:25:44,030 --> 00:25:45,640
Are you meeting someone after this?

558
00:25:48,390 --> 00:25:49,210
Ooh...

559
00:25:49,580 --> 00:25:52,490
Aha, so flustered you can't open the can.

560
00:25:53,290 --> 00:25:54,290
There.

561
00:25:54,310 --> 00:25:55,400
Suspish.

562
00:25:55,610 --> 00:25:56,920
Cheers, Sarge.

563
00:25:57,980 --> 00:25:59,210
Bottoms up.

564
00:25:59,390 --> 00:26:00,570
You're gonna get it hard.

565
00:26:00,590 --> 00:26:01,670
Who's the one?

566
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:09,390
Why are you downing it so fast?

567
00:26:09,840 --> 00:26:10,840
In a hurry?

568
00:26:11,290 --> 00:26:12,400
I'm just teasing ya.

569
00:26:15,250 --> 00:26:16,640
If I drink that fast,

570
00:26:16,990 --> 00:26:18,690
Priew's mama is gonna get some.

571
00:26:20,580 --> 00:26:21,800
We'll rock all four bed legs.

572
00:26:22,090 --> 00:26:23,910
It's gonna sound like
a real slaughterhouse.

573
00:26:25,190 --> 00:26:26,380
If you walk past my room,

574
00:26:27,280 --> 00:26:29,350
someone will be crying out to God,
even though we're not Christians.

575
00:26:43,240 --> 00:26:44,180
Not asking you to pitch in more than 500.

576
00:26:45,070 --> 00:26:46,180
You've already downed all my beers.

577
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:25,000
Hey,

578
00:27:26,220 --> 00:27:28,380
are you mad at me about this morning?

579
00:27:29,090 --> 00:27:30,090
Hm?

580
00:27:33,390 --> 00:27:34,890
You're not answering.

581
00:27:41,110 --> 00:27:42,460
I was...

582
00:27:42,610 --> 00:27:44,160
just unsure.

583
00:27:45,290 --> 00:27:46,890
Seek your bed, Lieutenant.

584
00:27:46,990 --> 00:27:48,200
It is well into the night.

585
00:27:54,680 --> 00:27:56,780
Are you avoiding me on purpose?

586
00:27:57,190 --> 00:27:57,910
Huh?

587
00:28:03,590 --> 00:28:05,540
Someone like myself does not avoid others,

588
00:28:06,100 --> 00:28:09,380
but I cannot share a bed
with someone who is intoxicated,

589
00:28:09,920 --> 00:28:13,390
nor can I bind my life
to someone of different morals.

590
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:20,530
I do not wish
to hold you against your will.

591
00:28:21,990 --> 00:28:23,390
I'm sorry.

592
00:28:24,800 --> 00:28:26,600
I didn't think that...

593
00:28:28,170 --> 00:28:32,360
something like this
would hurt you this much.

594
00:28:32,990 --> 00:28:33,990
I'm sorry.

595
00:28:35,290 --> 00:28:36,770
I love;

596
00:28:36,790 --> 00:28:38,400
therefore, I am troubled.

597
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:40,240
Mortal or immortal,

598
00:28:40,260 --> 00:28:41,800
I do not wish for anyone
to brush against you.

599
00:28:42,390 --> 00:28:44,950
I yearn for you to be mine alone to claim.

600
00:28:48,520 --> 00:28:51,160
As for me,
I remain unpledged to anyone,

601
00:28:52,580 --> 00:28:54,600
lingering to be claimed

602
00:28:54,620 --> 00:28:56,110
by my lover.

603
00:28:56,900 --> 00:28:57,900
Well, well, well.

604
00:28:58,210 --> 00:29:00,470
- Are you...
- We will talk tomorrow.

605
00:29:01,500 --> 00:29:03,900
Seek a good night's rest.

606
00:29:04,490 --> 00:29:05,870
I will sleep in the prayer room.

607
00:29:06,810 --> 00:29:07,810
What?

608
00:29:19,100 --> 00:29:20,280
That's a total miss.

609
00:29:22,210 --> 00:29:23,560
My spit flew out.

610
00:29:24,760 --> 00:29:26,750
She didn't even finish wiping me down.

611
00:29:36,800 --> 00:29:39,010
All I did was skip breakfast with her.

612
00:29:39,790 --> 00:29:42,180
Is she really that furious?

613
00:29:55,640 --> 00:29:57,080
What do you want?

614
00:29:57,100 --> 00:29:58,100
Bullets.

615
00:29:59,090 --> 00:30:00,170
I need bullets

616
00:30:00,190 --> 00:30:02,590
that can stop invulnerable criminals
with impenetrable skin,

617
00:30:02,930 --> 00:30:05,110
the kind who practice
black magic like you do.

618
00:30:17,390 --> 00:30:21,360
[Treatise on War: Great Weapons of War]

619
00:30:28,270 --> 00:30:32,680
[Bullet Consecration Ritual]

620
00:30:32,700 --> 00:30:37,070
[Consecration Materials]

621
00:31:03,300 --> 00:31:04,300
I'm late.

622
00:31:37,420 --> 00:31:38,420
Mm.

623
00:31:39,830 --> 00:31:42,480
She's probably back at her sanctum.

624
00:32:25,390 --> 00:32:26,780
Just have a taste.

625
00:32:27,710 --> 00:32:29,250
I'm good.

626
00:32:29,290 --> 00:32:30,570
It'll be such a waste.

627
00:32:31,200 --> 00:32:32,200
My dearest,

628
00:32:33,200 --> 00:32:35,300
stay here with me.

629
00:33:05,100 --> 00:33:06,100
I will request the officer on duty

630
00:33:06,700 --> 00:33:08,070
to summarize the case file
and send it over ASAP.

631
00:33:08,490 --> 00:33:09,790
This case is quite sensitive.

632
00:33:12,990 --> 00:33:13,990
Of course.

633
00:33:14,980 --> 00:33:16,800
I'd like the evidence to be more solid.

634
00:33:19,700 --> 00:33:20,700
Sure.

635
00:33:21,570 --> 00:33:23,080
I'll send it over ASAP.

636
00:33:36,290 --> 00:33:37,910
What are these photos?

637
00:33:39,090 --> 00:33:41,090
These photos confirm clues about Krating.

638
00:33:41,490 --> 00:33:43,280
Right now, the guy
is hiding out in Mae Sot.

639
00:33:44,390 --> 00:33:46,860
So why haven't you
told me about this, sir?

640
00:33:48,400 --> 00:33:52,170
I have no obligation to report
this matter to my subordinates.

641
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:53,880
Besides, this matter

642
00:33:53,900 --> 00:33:56,070
is outside our jurisdiction.

643
00:33:56,090 --> 00:33:57,830
Let Mae Sot Police Station handle it.

644
00:33:58,580 --> 00:34:01,160
But I'm here for this case.

645
00:34:01,180 --> 00:34:02,230
You know that.

646
00:34:02,780 --> 00:34:03,990
All I know is that

647
00:34:04,400 --> 00:34:05,990
you can't be harmed,

648
00:34:07,090 --> 00:34:08,900
so do as I say.

649
00:34:09,810 --> 00:34:10,810
Let the local police

650
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:13,630
handle this matter.

651
00:34:16,690 --> 00:34:18,580
If you're done here, be on your way.

652
00:34:40,010 --> 00:34:40,780
Oh.

653
00:34:41,400 --> 00:34:41,990
How are you, Lieutenant?

654
00:34:43,590 --> 00:34:45,080
Where did you sleep last night?

655
00:34:46,890 --> 00:34:47,690
Huh?

656
00:34:52,860 --> 00:34:53,560
Lieutenant, what's the matter?

657
00:34:56,790 --> 00:34:58,210
Lieutenant, Lieutenant.

658
00:34:58,230 --> 00:34:59,300
Calm down.

659
00:35:00,030 --> 00:35:01,280
Take it easy, Lieutenant.

660
00:35:01,710 --> 00:35:02,710
What's going on?

661
00:35:12,680 --> 00:35:15,700
The chief knew about the clues
and kept them from me, Sarge.

662
00:35:16,600 --> 00:35:18,540
He doesn't want me
to investigate the case.

663
00:35:20,850 --> 00:35:21,790
What does that mean?

664
00:35:22,200 --> 00:35:24,100
My family urged him

665
00:35:24,520 --> 00:35:25,890
to make sure I stayed safe.

666
00:35:26,790 --> 00:35:30,540
But I came here specifically
to investigate the case, Sarge.

667
00:35:32,100 --> 00:35:33,100
I know that well.

668
00:35:34,400 --> 00:35:35,600
So what are you gonna do next?

669
00:35:38,130 --> 00:35:39,560
I'm going to Mae Sot.

670
00:35:41,200 --> 00:35:42,690
You're well-versed in the area, right?

671
00:35:43,020 --> 00:35:44,100
Wanna come with?

672
00:35:44,360 --> 00:35:45,550
I'm not that well-versed.

673
00:35:45,570 --> 00:35:47,600
But at least you know the area
better than I do.

674
00:35:49,420 --> 00:35:50,750
So what are you gonna say?

675
00:35:50,770 --> 00:35:51,860
Are you coming or not?

676
00:35:52,610 --> 00:35:53,280
Fine, I'm coming.

677
00:36:00,330 --> 00:36:04,160
[Mae Sot, Tak]

678
00:36:04,700 --> 00:36:05,700
Hello.

679
00:36:07,500 --> 00:36:08,950
- Hello, Auntie.
- Uh...

680
00:36:08,970 --> 00:36:10,000
May I ask you some questions?

681
00:36:10,720 --> 00:36:12,710
Have you seen, uh...

682
00:36:12,730 --> 00:36:14,410
a man around...

683
00:36:14,430 --> 00:36:15,290
170 cm tall.

684
00:36:15,310 --> 00:36:16,310
170

685
00:36:16,700 --> 00:36:19,280
He's a little tanned and sturdy.

686
00:36:19,300 --> 00:36:20,300
Have you seen him?

687
00:36:20,330 --> 00:36:21,870
I don't think so.

688
00:36:22,900 --> 00:36:23,630
Hello.

689
00:36:23,790 --> 00:36:27,590
Have you seen a man around 170 cm tall?

690
00:36:28,400 --> 00:36:29,890
Uh, never.

691
00:36:33,790 --> 00:36:34,490
Sarge.

692
00:36:34,510 --> 00:36:35,140
Yes?

693
00:36:35,320 --> 00:36:36,500
I see a security camera there.

694
00:36:37,530 --> 00:36:38,910
There's one.

695
00:36:39,700 --> 00:36:40,700
Yes, ma'am.

696
00:36:40,980 --> 00:36:43,210
I will liaise with Mae Sot Police Station.

697
00:36:43,980 --> 00:36:45,380
- Please do, Sarge.
- Yes, ma'am.

698
00:36:46,290 --> 00:36:47,440
Let's have a meal now.

699
00:36:47,460 --> 00:36:48,820
The khao soi place over there is amazing.

700
00:36:48,840 --> 00:36:49,800
- Wanna go?
- Is it?

701
00:36:49,830 --> 00:36:50,790
Delicious food.

702
00:36:51,270 --> 00:36:52,710
Ordered three bowls just for myself.

703
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:03,400
That's to freshen you up.

704
00:37:03,980 --> 00:37:05,180
Thank you, Sarge.

705
00:37:17,340 --> 00:37:18,440
Are you tired, Sarge?

706
00:37:19,100 --> 00:37:20,780
All day,

707
00:37:20,990 --> 00:37:22,700
you've been drinking water nonstop.

708
00:37:24,760 --> 00:37:25,760
I'm hungover.

709
00:37:26,510 --> 00:37:27,690
After you left last night,

710
00:37:28,550 --> 00:37:30,200
I chugged two to two
and a half bottle on my own.

711
00:37:31,720 --> 00:37:32,350
Though

712
00:37:32,590 --> 00:37:35,670
drinking tons of water
can help flush the alcohol out.

713
00:37:38,590 --> 00:37:41,680
Can that really
help flush the alcohol out, Sarge?

714
00:37:41,700 --> 00:37:42,700
What?

715
00:37:42,890 --> 00:37:44,150
When you pee,

716
00:37:44,170 --> 00:37:46,050
it might just get diluted.

717
00:37:48,420 --> 00:37:50,750
Someone like myself does not avoid others,

718
00:37:51,090 --> 00:37:54,140
but I cannot share a bed
with someone who is intoxicated,

719
00:37:54,630 --> 00:37:57,950
nor can I bind my life
to someone of different morals.

720
00:38:00,260 --> 00:38:01,260
Right.

721
00:38:02,190 --> 00:38:03,190
From...

722
00:38:03,400 --> 00:38:05,090
what you've told me,

723
00:38:05,470 --> 00:38:07,750
I happen to know someone

724
00:38:07,770 --> 00:38:10,200
who can reach out to officers
at Mae Sot Police Station.

725
00:38:11,400 --> 00:38:12,730
Do you remember Chai,

726
00:38:12,980 --> 00:38:14,680
the guy who brought me desserts
at the municipal market?

727
00:38:16,310 --> 00:38:17,310
I do.

728
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:21,010
Chai's nephew is a police inspector
at Mae Sot Police Station.

729
00:38:21,720 --> 00:38:25,120
I think if he has any clues,
he'll probably send them to you.

730
00:38:26,910 --> 00:38:28,210
That'd be great.

731
00:38:28,590 --> 00:38:29,810
However,

732
00:38:29,830 --> 00:38:32,160
the chief can't find out about this

733
00:38:32,180 --> 00:38:34,470
until we know for sure...

734
00:38:34,490 --> 00:38:36,720
that we can access them.

735
00:38:37,930 --> 00:38:38,640
Yes, ma'am.

736
00:38:40,910 --> 00:38:41,910
Ugh...

737
00:38:42,880 --> 00:38:43,780
Jeez,

738
00:38:43,800 --> 00:38:44,910
I'm hungry!

739
00:38:45,530 --> 00:38:47,300
When will we ever get to eat?

740
00:38:47,780 --> 00:38:49,590
Coming, officers.

741
00:38:49,610 --> 00:38:50,670
Jeez!

742
00:38:50,780 --> 00:38:53,240
Jeez, how impatient of you.

743
00:38:53,260 --> 00:38:54,620
We put in our order half an hour ago.

744
00:38:54,640 --> 00:38:55,590
Yes, your food is ready.

745
00:38:55,620 --> 00:38:57,000
This is made with a special recipe.

746
00:38:57,030 --> 00:38:58,190
- What recipe?
- Right.

747
00:38:58,210 --> 00:38:58,790
Uh...

748
00:38:58,810 --> 00:39:00,060
It's chicken khao soi

749
00:39:00,090 --> 00:39:01,510
for those who like to khao-slam at night.

750
00:39:01,950 --> 00:39:03,400
- Mm.
- Yeah, just go if you can't crack a joke.

751
00:39:04,360 --> 00:39:05,060
Right.

752
00:39:05,770 --> 00:39:08,120
Whenever I eat this, I think of my mom

753
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:10,310
because she does it better.

754
00:39:12,170 --> 00:39:12,650
Right.

755
00:39:12,670 --> 00:39:14,010
Give it a try, Lieutenant. It's tasty.

756
00:39:20,360 --> 00:39:21,420
Sarge,

757
00:39:21,440 --> 00:39:22,440
so many actors

758
00:39:22,480 --> 00:39:25,410
have visited this shop, though.

759
00:39:25,570 --> 00:39:27,890
They take photos of everyone who comes in.

760
00:39:27,910 --> 00:39:28,910
It's just to promote the shop.

761
00:39:59,300 --> 00:40:00,190
Sarge,

762
00:40:00,220 --> 00:40:02,450
please liaise with them
for security footage

763
00:40:02,470 --> 00:40:04,220
dating back two to three days, and...

764
00:40:04,240 --> 00:40:07,110
also get footage from the stores
and the neighborhood around here.

765
00:40:07,650 --> 00:40:09,500
Yes, ma'am. I'll get right to it.

766
00:40:11,810 --> 00:40:13,310
And if possible...

767
00:40:13,860 --> 00:40:15,970
I'd like to get to know Inspector Chon,

768
00:40:15,990 --> 00:40:17,410
Chai's nephew you mentioned.

769
00:40:17,430 --> 00:40:19,200
Could you ask him to meet me?

770
00:40:19,690 --> 00:40:20,560
Yes, ma'am.

771
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:23,400
Thank you so much
for always helping me, Sarge.

772
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:26,270
If something happens in the future,

773
00:40:26,290 --> 00:40:29,080
I promise I'll take full responsibility.

774
00:40:31,450 --> 00:40:33,290
I admire what a ball of fire you are,

775
00:40:34,850 --> 00:40:37,640
so tenacious about this case.

776
00:40:38,370 --> 00:40:40,630
But I do want you to understand

777
00:40:40,650 --> 00:40:43,190
that your life should be your priority.

778
00:40:44,610 --> 00:40:46,390
And I don't want you to think...

779
00:40:46,410 --> 00:40:47,720
that a life for a life

780
00:40:48,190 --> 00:40:49,570
is the right way to go.

781
00:40:57,500 --> 00:41:00,240
Thank you for your concern, Sarge.

782
00:41:04,140 --> 00:41:05,000
I think

783
00:41:05,490 --> 00:41:07,380
we could still make it
in time if we leave now.

784
00:41:08,930 --> 00:41:10,810
Where to?

785
00:41:11,070 --> 00:41:12,290
To the Master's sanctum, of course.

786
00:41:12,610 --> 00:41:13,980
If we leave now for Phop Phra,

787
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:16,000
the sanctum should still be open.

788
00:41:18,530 --> 00:41:21,180
So why are we...

789
00:41:21,210 --> 00:41:22,210
going to her sanctum?

790
00:41:22,350 --> 00:41:22,990
Good grief.

791
00:41:23,590 --> 00:41:24,590
You told me

792
00:41:24,610 --> 00:41:25,900
you were interested in the great charm,

793
00:41:25,920 --> 00:41:27,840
so I asked my wife to book an appointment.

794
00:41:31,390 --> 00:41:32,780
You've got it all wrong, Sarge.

795
00:41:32,940 --> 00:41:35,700
I'm not looking to get anything done.

796
00:41:35,720 --> 00:41:37,190
The reason I asked you

797
00:41:37,220 --> 00:41:41,190
is just to get some general information.

798
00:41:41,410 --> 00:41:42,410
Aha.

799
00:41:42,600 --> 00:41:43,600
Let's just go.

800
00:41:43,800 --> 00:41:44,750
It's already been booked, anyway.

801
00:41:45,620 --> 00:41:47,380
Just go and meet her for once,

802
00:41:47,730 --> 00:41:48,900
or else I'll lose face.

803
00:41:48,920 --> 00:41:50,110
Come on, get in the car.

804
00:41:50,520 --> 00:41:51,190
Come on!

805
00:41:51,620 --> 00:41:52,530
Chop-chop.

806
00:41:52,810 --> 00:41:53,650
Sarge!

807
00:41:53,670 --> 00:41:55,230
- Come on.
- If you wanna go, go by yourself.

808
00:41:55,250 --> 00:41:56,300
Nah!

809
00:41:59,520 --> 00:42:00,520
Lieutenant.

810
00:42:01,010 --> 00:42:02,190
Wrong car, Sarge!

811
00:42:04,070 --> 00:42:05,070
Open the door, Lieutenant.

812
00:42:07,890 --> 00:42:09,310
Why aren't you driving?

813
00:42:09,330 --> 00:42:10,740
I'm too lazy to drive, Lieutenant.

814
00:42:14,600 --> 00:42:16,290
I'll be going now, Master.

815
00:42:21,070 --> 00:42:21,910
Lieutenant.

816
00:42:23,440 --> 00:42:24,840
Go to her.

817
00:42:26,520 --> 00:42:27,530
Don't be afraid.

818
00:42:29,600 --> 00:42:31,090
I'm not afraid, Sarge.

819
00:42:31,700 --> 00:42:34,090
I'm not looking to get anything done.

820
00:42:34,490 --> 00:42:36,590
I'm just accompanying you.

821
00:42:36,610 --> 00:42:37,490
What?

822
00:42:37,520 --> 00:42:39,000
Go on. You're already here, anyway.

823
00:42:39,200 --> 00:42:41,100
You have arrived at my sanctum.

824
00:42:41,790 --> 00:42:44,140
How could you depart empty-handed?

825
00:42:45,930 --> 00:42:46,650
Come.

826
00:42:46,920 --> 00:42:48,900
Let me incant a verse upon you,

827
00:42:49,300 --> 00:42:51,500
and you can decide then.

828
00:42:52,300 --> 00:42:53,300
Go.

829
00:42:55,230 --> 00:42:56,230
Go.

830
00:42:56,800 --> 00:42:58,180
- What?
- Alright, Sarge.

831
00:42:58,200 --> 00:42:59,200
Go now.

832
00:43:15,490 --> 00:43:17,270
Whatever clouded your mind,

833
00:43:17,720 --> 00:43:20,740
has it been warded off by the alcohol?

834
00:43:24,310 --> 00:43:26,780
I won't cause you trouble

835
00:43:27,700 --> 00:43:29,600
like I did last night.

836
00:43:32,390 --> 00:43:33,300
Come.

837
00:43:34,320 --> 00:43:36,660
Let me see your face up close.

838
00:43:55,400 --> 00:43:56,400
Closer.

839
00:44:57,980 --> 00:45:00,300
Know you of the Sattabut lotus?

840
00:45:35,230 --> 00:45:36,720
Pray you, take your leave.

841
00:45:36,890 --> 00:45:39,330
The ritual I shall perform
upon the lieutenant

842
00:45:39,350 --> 00:45:40,280
will last long.

843
00:46:08,880 --> 00:46:10,990
Since you scorn these rituals,

844
00:46:11,370 --> 00:46:13,800
I have never thought
to trouble you with one.

845
00:46:16,990 --> 00:46:18,790
For someone like me,

846
00:46:19,400 --> 00:46:21,290
should I wish to have anyone
enamored of me,

847
00:46:34,690 --> 00:46:36,610
my beauty alone

848
00:46:37,710 --> 00:46:38,990
would suffice...

849
00:47:06,680 --> 00:47:08,720
At every sunrise and nightfall,
I yearn for you, my dearest.

850
00:47:09,470 --> 00:47:11,350
That is why last night was such a torment

851
00:47:11,710 --> 00:47:13,720
Do you not feel as I do?

852
00:47:16,410 --> 00:47:18,640
Then, we should spend the night together.

853
00:47:19,300 --> 00:47:21,770
Let me be the one to pleasure you

854
00:47:22,900 --> 00:47:26,380
until I ease what torments you.

855
00:50:20,740 --> 00:50:22,580
What you need, my dearest,

856
00:50:22,600 --> 00:50:24,800
is not something
that may be done with ease.

857
00:50:25,600 --> 00:50:27,520
Perils will come your way

858
00:50:28,000 --> 00:50:29,800
from the very instant
you seek the sacred materials.

859
00:50:31,130 --> 00:50:33,190
I'm not afraid of evil.

860
00:50:35,910 --> 00:50:38,390
Should you be determined
to make consecrated bullets,

861
00:50:38,770 --> 00:50:40,670
always bear in mind the virtues

862
00:50:41,400 --> 00:50:43,570
and faith in good deeds.

863
00:50:43,590 --> 00:50:45,300
Though you do not hold them
close to your heart,

864
00:50:45,320 --> 00:50:47,070
dare not desecrate them.

865
00:50:49,790 --> 00:50:52,150
I'm here to uphold justice.

866
00:50:52,590 --> 00:50:55,610
Though I can't let go of all my vengeance,

867
00:50:56,080 --> 00:50:59,050
I would never want to
desecrate anyone's faith.

868
00:51:01,210 --> 00:51:03,300
I have faith in

869
00:51:03,590 --> 00:51:06,470
the teachings of Buddhism.

870
00:51:18,900 --> 00:51:21,110
I pray that you

871
00:51:21,600 --> 00:51:24,160
guide my good intentions

872
00:51:24,320 --> 00:51:26,100
to success.

873
00:52:02,990 --> 00:52:03,870
My dearest,

874
00:52:04,600 --> 00:52:05,910
come to me.

875
00:52:29,190 --> 00:52:31,370
Wear this upon you.

876
00:52:31,390 --> 00:52:33,390
Do not give it to anyone so readily again.

877
00:52:39,010 --> 00:52:41,670
May the sacred beings watch over you

878
00:52:42,790 --> 00:52:45,370
until your good intentions

879
00:52:45,990 --> 00:52:48,270
prevail.

880
00:52:52,480 --> 00:52:53,480
Yes,

881
00:52:54,000 --> 00:52:55,000
Master.

882
00:52:57,620 --> 00:52:59,690
Do I have to call you...

883
00:52:59,720 --> 00:53:02,010
"Master," like everyone else does?

884
00:53:02,280 --> 00:53:05,590
You neither embrace
nor believe in what I am.

885
00:53:05,800 --> 00:53:07,290
No need to address me as others do.

886
00:53:08,640 --> 00:53:10,180
Then...

887
00:53:12,290 --> 00:53:13,600
Thank you,

888
00:53:15,480 --> 00:53:17,190
Master Bulan.

889
00:53:17,630 --> 00:53:21,550
♫Mantra of love, please take the lead♫

890
00:53:21,570 --> 00:53:26,390
♫So our hearts are sworn by♫

891
00:53:26,410 --> 00:53:29,310
♫I shall love and commit♫

892
00:53:29,330 --> 00:53:33,030
♫Until the day I die♫

893
00:53:33,330 --> 00:53:37,470
♫As long as I shall breathe♫

894
00:53:37,490 --> 00:53:40,930
♫I will be your karmic soulmate♫

895
00:53:40,950 --> 00:53:46,150
♫Until my being fades♫

896
00:53:46,650 --> 00:53:52,930
♫May sacred mantras bind us together♫

897
00:53:59,440 --> 00:54:01,590
This is Inspector Chon,

898
00:54:01,990 --> 00:54:03,500
stationed at Mae Sot Police Station.

899
00:54:03,790 --> 00:54:05,870
From the clues I've gathered in secret,

900
00:54:06,400 --> 00:54:08,270
Krating and his guys

901
00:54:08,300 --> 00:54:11,360
are moving along
the Thailand-Myanmar border.

902
00:54:11,520 --> 00:54:14,490
If the person
you're waiting for isn't me...

903
00:54:14,510 --> 00:54:16,400
you can be honest.

904
00:54:19,390 --> 00:54:21,370
As you gather the sacred materials,

905
00:54:21,390 --> 00:54:23,590
the Buddha's virtues
shall spread far and wide.

906
00:54:23,610 --> 00:54:26,080
Restless spirits and ghosts shall storm in.

907
00:54:44,380 --> 00:54:47,760
♫It's not that I don't feel it♫

908
00:54:47,790 --> 00:54:51,560
♫It's not that I'm cold-hearted♫

909
00:54:51,580 --> 00:54:55,190
♫For the love you've given♫

910
00:54:58,290 --> 00:55:01,590
♫It's because it feels too good to be true,♫

911
00:55:01,760 --> 00:55:05,070
♫So much so that I doubt if it's true♫

912
00:55:05,260 --> 00:55:11,990
♫If it's smoke and mirrors,
a dream that lingers♫

913
00:55:12,040 --> 00:55:17,700
♫Deeply swayed by love,
all while shaken with dread,♫

914
00:55:18,110 --> 00:55:24,260
♫Scared that it's not love
after all in the end♫

915
00:55:25,530 --> 00:55:30,160
♫What if, between us,♫

916
00:55:30,440 --> 00:55:35,710
♫It's nothing but a perfect illusion,♫

917
